{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1243700-how-often-do-you-delay-your-action-to-attempt-a-clash","id":1243700,"title":"How often do you delay your action to attempt a clash?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-08-07T21:21:46-07:00","id":1243700,"title":"How often do you delay your action to attempt a clash?","content":"This question is especially for players whose characters use two-handed heavy weapons, with their clash bonus and low Accuracy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-07T21:50:36-07:00","id":1243705,"title":"","content":"Not nearly enough","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-07T22:04:28-07:00","id":1243708,"title":"","content":"Because of its weapon, the tetsubo/grand goremaul, a martial artist of Earth Dragon Style always has the option to knock a target down or away. The Form Charm specifically improves the accuracy of the inaccurate weapon when making smash attacks or attacking prone targets, encouraging the martial artist to knock the target down and keep hammering them while they're down, but it shouldn't be forgotten that the martial artist can also simply strike with her body for more accurate attacks that lack the costs of smash attacks, and these unarmed attacks could include the Charms of other Styles. If these unarmed attacks (such as stomps) are made against a prone target, they are even more accurate.<br /> <br /> (By &quot;accurate&quot;, I mean that the Charms make it cheaper to max out your dice-pools; they don't actually break your dice-cap or do anything to make your dice more effective.)<br /> <br /> But in order to further increase the odds of landing a hit with the hammer, the martial artist can delay her action to attempt to force a clashing smash attack. This could allow her to succeed with Stillness-of-Stone Atemi (especially backed up with Force of the Mountain, and possibly Hungry Earth Strike). Succeeding with that withering attack could then allow her to launch an Avalanche Method (also backed up with Force of the Mountain for each attack) in the next round before her target gets a chance to act (such as rising from prone or breaking out of Hungry Earth Strike's prison), and before his mobility penalty wears off, even if she doesn't drive him into crash.<br /> <br /> Plus, when the martial artist does decide to risk a failed clash attack's punishment (including an Onslaught penalty) <i>and </i>an attempted smash attack's Defense penalty, her Style allows the heaviest of armor <i>and</i> provides up to four Charms for soaking attacks, reflecting a great deal of caution.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, she could potentially reduce her Defense to 0 with multiple smashing attacks through Avalanche Method. Also, using even one smash attack (let alone the three or four successful smashing attacks necessary to cause any falling damage) would more quickly lower Avalanche Method's decisive damage pool, as each one costs 2 Initiative to attempt. This is why it helps that no single attack will have less than base Initiative damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 08-09-2019, 10:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-07T22:32:36-07:00","id":1243710,"title":"","content":"Fire Dragon Style uses light-weight weapons, but since they are paired, the you get the same +2 clash bonus. While the Style also allows unarmed attacks which enables you to mix Styles, short daiklaves offer objectively superior traits for pure Fire Dragon attacks.<br /> <br /> Flash-Fire Technique helps you act first, giving you the option of delaying your action to attempt to force a clash with some of the best basic accuracy in the game. Your enemy's two-handed hammer's greater damage means nothing if you win the attack roll contest.<br /> <br /> But your opponent wouldn't have to worry about the preemptive onslaught penalty imposed by Fire Dragon Form.<br /> <br /> Overwhelming Fire Majesty Stance makes it even harder for you to fail a clash, and also offers the Style's only precaution against a failed clash attack, aside from the limited allowance on armor. Inflicting one dice of Hardness-ignoring lethal damage isn't a very fair trade for potentially dying, though. Consuming Might of the Fire Dragon improves this &quot;defense&quot;, but not enough to risk your life for it.<br /> <br /> By delaying your action to clash with a withering attack, you may strike with Searing Edge Attack, destroying your opponent's Initiative as well as stealing it. But since your Initiative was already higher before you succeeded on this withering attack, the tactical situation doesn't change all that much.<br /> <br /> Breath of the Fire Dragon is unblockable; there's no reason to ever delay using this attack.<br /> <br /> <br /> In conclusion, this Style really doesn't support the tactic of delaying actions, given how its Charms enable and reward attacking immediately, before your opponent can act, and then parrying attacks if your opponent survived. These same parrying Charms likewise don't support the practice of protecting yourself with a clash attack, which is probably why the Style has nothing like Earth Dragon's Weapon-Breaking Defense Technique.<br /> <br /> Fire Dragon Style also has nothing like the combination of Stillness-of-Stone Atemi (which creates a potentially short window of opportunity) and Avalanche Method (which absolutely requires a potentially short window of opportunity). Earth Dragon Style has a theme of setting up a singular, momentarily perfect situation in which the target is utterly helpless and thoroughly screwed.<br /> <br /> By contrast, Fire Dragon is about immediately and relentlessly fucking up someone's shit from the word &quot;Go&quot;. Therefore, there's little incentive to delay for a withering attack that lets one launch a decisive attack before the opponent's turn in the next round.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 08-09-2019, 10:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-07T23:02:44-07:00","id":1243716,"title":"","content":"For some reason, White Reaper Style now allows unarmed attacks. These offer one point more Accuracy than artifact spears, but probably cannot grapple with this Ability. Neither weapon offers a Clash bonus. Spears offer a +1 Defense bonus.<br /> <br /> But if one wants to use the heavy-weight lances and scythes allowed by the style, Accuracy is low, and the Two-Handed tag definitely grants the clash bonus.<br /> <br /> White Reaper does allow the heaviest of armor and includes a soak-enhancing Charm, allowing one some protection against failed clash attacks. But the Style also offers two parry-enhancing Charms, while lacking a reflexive clash defense Charm, so clashing isn't necessarily the Style's best defense.<br /> <br /> Bleeding Crescent Strike works just as well for a normal attack as for a clash. Beware if you want to use Falling Scythe Flash for a decisive clash (with or without Bleeding Crescent Strike), as losing two points of Initiative by delaying your action could bring your Initiative total equal to your target's, and thus disqualify using the Charm against them.<br /> <br /> Like Fire Dragon Style, White Reaper lacks a &quot;Stillness-of-Stone Atemi / Avalanche Method&quot; duo of &quot;set-up and super-attack&quot;, and has no native way to knock a target prone. There's little incentive to delay a withering attack for the purpose of clashing and then attacking before the target can act on the next round, so the only point of delaying your action is when you're confident that you can use your heaviest weapon to beat someone's best attack rather than their best defense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 08-09-2019, 10:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-08T05:38:18-07:00","id":1243762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1243700-how-often-do-you-delay-your-action-to-attempt-a-clash?p=1243716#post1243716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For some reason, White Reaper Style <b>now</b> allows unarmed attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>You say that like White Reaper hasn't <i>always</i> allowed unarmed attacks.<br /> <br /> To answer your central question* though: I don't play many combat-centric PCs, assuming I'm not the ST, so I have yet to do it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ______________<br /> *Which I initially thought was rhetorical, given the way you launched into tactical analyses of the different Martial Arts styles, right up until I got your Visitor Message.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 08-08-2018, 10:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-08T08:34:02-07:00","id":1243805,"title":"","content":"Almost always whenever my intended target has less Initiative than me. But then again my character uses paired short artifact weapons which is literally the highest possible base accuracy for a withering attack in the game","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-08T08:54:32-07:00","id":1243811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadassOverlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1243700-how-often-do-you-delay-your-action-to-attempt-a-clash?p=1243805#post1243805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Almost always whenever my intended target has less Initiative than me. But then again my character uses paired short artifact weapons which is literally the highest possible base accuracy for a withering attack in the game</div> </div> </div> </div>I do want to look at Mantis and Tiger Styles next, for that reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-08T10:23:16-07:00","id":1243840,"title":"","content":"Very often.<br /> <br /> I have defense penalties? Time to delay, clashes don't care about onslaught, and wound penalties are effectively halved.<br /> <br /> They're laboring under a penalty to rolled actions? Time to delay, I'm better off hitting their penalized attack than their unmodified defense.<br /> <br /> I have trouble with their soak or they're down to their last health level and I don't have the initiative to reliably finish them? Clash damage bonuses may solve the issue.<br /> <br /> Applying a -2 Defense penalty from losing a clash before my big decisive next turn is also supremely useful.<br /> <br /> And then you have the sheer psychological impact of saying &quot;I delay my action&quot; when you have a sufficiently large bonus relative to your opponent - you can often force them to avoid attacking entirely, without having to give up much in return (the initiative from delaying is lost, sure, but you can always just do your attack after they're done with their turn).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-08T12:24:59-07:00","id":1243885,"title":"","content":"Hardly ever, but I really should, as I'm using two short daiklaives. It kind of feels a bit risky though, to throw away 2i, when they might not even attack you. Though I guess you can then just stab them anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-08T12:32:05-07:00","id":1243886,"title":"","content":"How many motes would you be willing to spend to keep those Initiative points?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-08T13:03:33-07:00","id":1243902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1243700-how-often-do-you-delay-your-action-to-attempt-a-clash?p=1243885#post1243885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hardly ever, but I really should, as I'm using two short daiklaives. It kind of feels a bit risky though, to throw away 2i, when they might not even attack you. Though I guess you can then just stab them anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something you can always do is try to be an arrogant dick during the combat and make them WANT to attack you, even if they shouldn\u2019t. I think that\u2019s basically what fire aspects are built to do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1243700-how-often-do-you-delay-your-action-to-attempt-a-clash?p=1243886#post1243886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many motes would you be willing to spend to keep those Initiative points?</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s a very good question. Would it be a blanket save motes to delay for any reason, or only to clash?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-08T13:13:04-07:00","id":1243905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1243700-how-often-do-you-delay-your-action-to-attempt-a-clash?p=1243902#post1243902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something you can always do is try to be an arrogant dick during the combat and make them WANT to attack you, even if they shouldn\u2019t. I think that\u2019s basically what fire aspects are built to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That\u2019s a very good question. Would it be a blanket save motes to delay for any reason, or only to clash? </div> </div> </div>Answer for both questions, please.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-08T13:16:29-07:00","id":1243907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1243700-how-often-do-you-delay-your-action-to-attempt-a-clash?p=1243886#post1243886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many motes would you be willing to spend to keep those Initiative points?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmmm... 3 or 4 maybe?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-08T13:18:41-07:00","id":1243908,"title":"","content":"1m for 1i is generally a decent, if not outstandingly good deal (see also: Reed in the Wind).<br /> <br /> Are you asking how much is the maximum I'd be willing to pay to retain 2i? How much would make me very happy to have the ability?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-08T13:28:08-07:00","id":1243912,"title":"","content":"I think I'd expect a charm (which cost 8/10xp, so should be better than parity) that says &quot;you may activate this charm when delaying to waive the 2i cost of delaying&quot; to cost 2 or 3m. I'd be willing to buy it for a character who often delays if it cost 4m. I think if it cost 5m+, I'd consider it a poor deal and wouldn't bother buying it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-08T13:39:31-07:00","id":1243916,"title":"","content":"What if you could use a reflexive movement action and then still delay your attack for the round?<br /> <br /> Or if you could not only delay your attack, but the longer you delayed, the better your attack becomes... though being attacked beforehand would cancel the bonus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-08T14:00:54-07:00","id":1243923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1243700-how-often-do-you-delay-your-action-to-attempt-a-clash?p=1243916#post1243916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if you could use a reflexive movement action and then still delay your attack for the round?<br /> <br /> Or if you could not only delay your attack, but the longer you delayed, the better your attack becomes... though being attacked beforehand would cancel the bonus.</div> </div> </div> </div>That might be a bit much bookkeeping, but I'm not sure.<br /> <br /> For my answer I might have a Solar go 1-2 motes for a delay to clash only, 2-3 motes for a general delay. For a DB 2-3 motes for a delay to clash only.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-08T14:04:31-07:00","id":1243924,"title":"","content":"The character I did a lot of my practice combats with is a Steel Devil martial artist with paired short daiklaves, so delaying was a fairly frequent tactic in those trials. While I don't have the math to prove it, my impression was the 2i spent to delay was more than paid back by the extra attack dice on the clash and how they interacted with the MA charms to deal more damage. Plus, y'know, motes I spent on the attack were also effectively increasing my Defense in single combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-08T14:15:08-07:00","id":1243926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1243700-how-often-do-you-delay-your-action-to-attempt-a-clash?p=1243902#post1243902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Something you can always do is try to be an arrogant dick during the combat and make them WANT to attack you, even if they shouldn\u2019t. I think that\u2019s basically what fire aspects are built to do.<br /> <br /> ...</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, ever since we first got the IMAs preview, and the talk that that happened about Fire Dragon and Steel Devil, that this sort of build keeps popping up in my head as the first DB I would like to play.<br /> <br /> I was rereading Fire Dragon Style, and the bit about it being trained along with dance caught my attention. I went to reread the Performance Charms and found Irresistible Whirlpool Diversion.<br /> <br /> How cool is that?<br /> <br /> JB - Get as high as possible Join Battle and channel all you can to your Offhand Charge.<br /> <br /> R1 - Activate Dual Slaying Stance.<br /> <br /> R2 - Start an anger inspiring, Irresistible Whirlpool Diversion backed, dance.<br /> <br /> R3 - Flurry full defense with continued performing.<br /> <br /> If you have one more round before starting the dance, you can activate Moth to the Candle.<br /> <br /> With this the dance will anger your foes and will make it very hard for them to pay attention to anything but you. If you have Moth to the Candle, even more so.<br /> <br /> If they attack you, through Dual Slaying Stance, you get a Decisive Counterattack that doesn't reset you to base.<br /> <br /> Dual Slaying Stance is almost an Excellency capped Parry (+2, DB maximum +3), you're in full defense (another +2 to Defense), but flurrying (-1 Defense, I seem to remember a flurry penalty negation for flurry with Social Influence, but i think it was restricted to Socialize and Presence, not sure though).<br /> <br /> If you had a high enough JB, one where even after offloading to OCharge you are still higher than your enemies, you can benefit short swords (light) and Flame-Flicker Stance, and also give your counters a bit more oomph with Perfect Blazing Blow.<br /> <br /> If not rock the (medium) swords and get that +1 parry off the bat.<br /> <br /> The more numerous the enemies the more FFS will shine.<br /> <br /> Depending on stats and luck, all of your enemies will want to attack you and everytime they do they'll get a 5-10 dice of damage Decisive to the face. Depending on rolls, that is 2-4 rounds to kill whatever number of enemies attacking you. While you are in drawing their attention away from whatever else and in an extremely strong defensive position.<br /> <br /> The aesthetics are also awesome, the whirlpool theme drawing the enemies to you to be pureed... I'm tempted to grant Three Swords Devil the sobriquet &quot;The Antlion&quot;.<br /> <br /> Bonus: Petal-Strewn Pavane will let you flurry movement actions with dancing without flurry penalties, so you can disengage and rush while keep dancing, baiting your enemies into traps and/or hazards, or closing in with ranged attackers when needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2746,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","user":"TGUEIROS","date":". 08-09-2018, 09:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-08T21:01:47-07:00","id":1244041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1243700-how-often-do-you-delay-your-action-to-attempt-a-clash?p=1243924#post1243924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The character I did a lot of my practice combats with is a Steel Devil martial artist with paired short daiklaves, so delaying was a fairly frequent tactic in those trials. While I don't have the math to prove it, my impression was the 2i spent to delay was more than paid back by the extra attack dice on the clash and how they interacted with the MA charms to deal more damage. Plus, y'know, motes I spent on the attack were also effectively increasing my Defense in single combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about when you're delaying to make a smash attack? You're losing a total of 4i.<br /> <br /> It's probably worth every point if it succeeds, but it's still expensive.<br /> <br /> When you're also using Stillness-of-Stone Atemi, you're spending even more Initiative than that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-08T23:35:43-07:00","id":1244059,"title":"","content":"Tiger Style has absolutely no parrying or evasion Charms. It only allows light armor, but includes a soak-enhancing Charm. Paired tiger claws and razor claws have no Defense bonus, the best basic clash attack accuracy in the game, and the Style is full of Charms for capitalizing on successful attacks and grapple gambits to inflict tremendous damage. Grappling someone penalizes their attack rolls by -1; by -3 if they use a two-handed weapon, which neatly neutralizes the clash bonus of two-handed melee weapons.<br /> <br /> Basically, whenever you have the Initiative advantage in a duel (whether an actual duel or a moment in which there's no one else within range of the two of you), you should always be delaying your action to force a clash. At least, if you mean to make a withering attack.<br /> <br /> Even when making a decisive clash attack (and therefore losing your accuracy bonus) paired tiger claws give you a +2 bonus to the attack roll. That's good enough to match the withering attack pool of a mundane medium or two-handed heavy weapon (the later of which because it is bringing its own +2 clash bonus).<br /> <br /> When faced with the prospect of attacking you and risking a clash, your lower-Initiative opponent may decide to try disengaging instead. If they do, Tiger Form basically refunds you the cost of delaying. Plus, even if they succeed, you can use your action to rush them, and Tiger Style has all sorts of tricks to chase after and then punish someone who ran away.<br /> <br /> Since Tiger Style includes a Charm to render a target prone, there's value in delaying to clash with a withering attack so that you can ensure you can act again in the next round before your target has a chance to stand back up. Any Exalt can use the follow-up attack to deliver Spine-Shattering Bite, which greatly complicates the target's ability to rise from prone. A Solar can use Raging Tiger Pounce's mastery level to make attacks against the prone target undodgeable; this can be multiple attacks, as shaking off the effects of Spine-Shattering Bite and rising from prone are two different actions. Reversing the effects of SSB also counts as disengaging, which renders the victim vulnerable to a number of nasty effects.<br /> <br /> Since Tiger Form renders the martial artist immune to the usual penalties of being prone (possibly including the inability to take movement actions, if I remember Robert's answer correctly), then a grand master martial artist never needs to relent in her assault if knocked down; she just drags her opponent down to her level and beats him with experience.<br /> <br /> <br /> We don't know if it's possible to delay your grappling action <i>after </i>successfully initiating a grapple. Naturally, this seems to only matter if you grappled the target immediately rather than as part of a successful clash forced by already delaying your action. But afterwards, it should be possible to delay your action so that you can clash your victim's attacks with savaging or throwing attacks.<br /> <br /> On the one hand, this actually gives them a way to defend against your savaging or throwing attacks when normally their Defense is completely inapplicable. On the other, if you win the clash with a savaging attack, they can't use their attack to reduce your rounds of control through inflicting damage (though you should still lose one round for being clashed at all).<br /> <br /> Losing rounds of control isn't a concern if you just want to throw your opponent. But delaying a withering throw is pretty much like delaying to make a non-grappling withering attack with Raging Tiger Pounce; if you succeed, your target is prone, can't act again until the next round, and you can attack in the next round before he can act.<br /> <br /> There's no point in delaying for a restrain action, which has no attack roll to clash with, and which renders the target incapable of acting anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 08-11-2018, 01:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T03:00:53-07:00","id":1244087,"title":"","content":"So far I've primarily played a non-combatant and a grappler in 3rd, but I sort of get inspired by this to make a character that wields a mirrored weapon which has evocations that plays with this mechanic by embodying patience and meeting force with force","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amateur drawsmith","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2847-thatsmellygoblin","name":"ThatSmellyGoblin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2847_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T05:24:55-07:00","id":1244098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1243700-how-often-do-you-delay-your-action-to-attempt-a-clash?p=1243926#post1243926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">R2 - Flurry Full Defense with an anger inspiring, Irresistible Whirlpool Diversion backed, dance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sadly, I don't think you can flurry Simple charms...<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T05:33:39-07:00","id":1244099,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m glad my thread is giving people new ideas.<br /> <br /> Are my Clash breakdowns of the Martial Arts Styles helpful or interesting at all?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T05:48:46-07:00","id":1244102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1243700-how-often-do-you-delay-your-action-to-attempt-a-clash#post1243700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This question is especially for players whose characters use two-handed heavy weapons, with their clash bonus and low Accuracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's probably going to factor heavily into &quot;how to play a Sidereal&quot; if their excellency still works anything like it does in the Ex3 core.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T06:54:47-07:00","id":1244121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1243700-how-often-do-you-delay-your-action-to-attempt-a-clash?p=1244098#post1244098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sadly, I don't think you can flurry Simple charms...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is true, I got a little mixed up with Petal-Strewn Pavane, which I was examining for Disengage and Rush while dancing.<br /> <br /> Though that doesn't change the essence of the actions, it only requires you to have another round of preparation, so the flurrying with the dance starts at R3.<br /> <br /> I will adjust the post for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T08:15:32-07:00","id":1244151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1243700-how-often-do-you-delay-your-action-to-attempt-a-clash?p=1244121#post1244121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is true, I got a little mixed up with Petal-Strewn Pavane, which I was examining for Disengage and Rush while dancing.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it matters, Robert is going to re-examine PSP after someone complained that it was too powerful compared to Dragon-Blooded Athletics and Dodge Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T08:16:28-07:00","id":1244152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1243700-how-often-do-you-delay-your-action-to-attempt-a-clash?p=1244102#post1244102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's probably going to factor heavily into &amp;quot;how to play a Sidereal&amp;quot; if their excellency still works anything like it does in the Ex3 core.</div> </div> </div> </div>I forget, how does it work and how do you see it factoring into this tactic?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T08:36:43-07:00","id":1244160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1243700-how-often-do-you-delay-your-action-to-attempt-a-clash?p=1244151#post1244151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If it matters, Robert is going to re-examine PSP after someone complained that it was too powerful compared to Dragon-Blooded Athletics and Dodge Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't know that it was going under revision, or paid any real attention as to how it compares to the other trees.<br /> <br /> I hope it doesn't get too downgraded, but we'll see!<br /> <br /> Thanks for the info!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2746,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","user":"TGUEIROS","date":". 08-09-2018, 11:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T10:36:35-07:00","id":1244198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1243700-how-often-do-you-delay-your-action-to-attempt-a-clash?p=1244152#post1244152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I forget, how does it work and how do you see it factoring into this tactic?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not the person this is asking, but my analysis of the corebook sidereal excellency and clashes:<br /> <br /> Sidereal excellency is 1m per die or target number reduction, max of (essence) dice and 3 target number reduction. 2m per static number increase, max (essence).<br /> At &gt;5 die pools, target number reduction is more efficient than dice adding, and for most possible essence/attribute/ability/other sources of dice the cap is higher than solars. (At e3+ the sidereal always has a higher cap for expected successes, at e1 or e2 a near max attribute+ability can beat the sidereal if there aren't many dice from stunt, speciality, accuracy, or similar coming in.)<br /> The static excellency, on the other hand, has the same efficiency as everyone else, and at low essence a pretty poor cap.<br /> <br /> This lets them do much better on rolls than other splats before charms, and often even after charms, especially on things like withering attacks with high-accuracy weapons. Clashes put a lot of focus on winning a single roll, can get a lot of non-charm dice from accuracy and dual wielding, and compensate for the sidereal's poor Defense cap.<br /> An e1, dex 5, ability 5, specialty sidereal dual wielding light artifact weapons in a clash with a 1-point stunt and max excellency averages 16.8 successes. And only spends 4m for this<br /> A solar under the same conditions averages 15, excellent strike brings that up to 16.556, for 10 or 11 motes.<br /> At higher essence this gets even more extreme - e5 gives 20 average successes for 8m.<br /> <br /> Because of this, a clash-specialized sidereal can win lots of clashes, even against other clash-specialized enemies, and won't need to spend as many motes.<br /> <br /> On another note, do people think Snake Form's penalty to attacks applies to clash attacks?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T11:12:45-07:00","id":1244210,"title":"","content":"Thanks.<br /> <br /> And any penalty to attacks applies to clashes unless explicitly stated otherwise.<br /> <br /> Does anyone want me to look into Snake Style after I finish with Mantis?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T11:32:20-07:00","id":1244219,"title":"","content":"Yes, as I might make a Snake Stylist in future, and my friend is playing one now.<br /> <br /> I admit, I didn't really think much about clashing with my Tiger Stylist, but you're right, defensively it's not great so clashing really does make sense. Though his initiative isn't that great (Join Battle 6, no excellency). Still, initiative's go up and down through combat.<br /> <br /> I don't quite agree that you should always delay and clash though. After all, if you want to make a decisive attack, and they clash you with a light withering attack, they may well have 4 more dice than you.<br /> <br /> Also, of course, in a fight with multiple people, they may attack someone else, at which point you attack them anyway, but wasted 2i.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T11:33:46-07:00","id":1244221,"title":"","content":"Mantis Style allows no armor, and its only soak enhancement requires you to attempt parrying, so it doesn't have any precaution against losing a clash. The form and a pre-form Charm boost your parry defense, and the Style allows you to use a seven-section staff which has a medium-weight class Defense bonus of 1.<br /> <br /> This could actually incentivize the martial artist (when not clinching) to delay until <i>after</i> his opponent acts, without clashing. She lets her opponent\u2019s attack crash against her Iron Arm Block and suffer an onslaught penalty that makes attacking him easier.<br /> <br /> (EDIT: A better idea is the Mantis stylist using a Full Defense to make sure Iron Arm Block works in the first place, and then attacking first in the next round before the attacker\u2019s new onslaught penalty disappears. It\u2019s the same gamble, but less risky and less expensive. Though delaying does have the advantage of letting the martial artist do anything else if her opponent decided to not attack at all.)<br /> <br /> However, all of the Style\u2019s other weapons are light-weight, with no Defense bonus. With the exception of nunchaku, they\u2019re all easily paired for a Clash bonus, and players probably have little difficulty getting most storytellers to let them pair nunchaku, thanks to <i>TMNT\u2019s</i> Michelangelo and <i>RWBY\u2019s</i> Sun Wukong.<br /> <br /> Clinching penalizes your opponent\u2019s attack dice, and Mantis Style really wants to clinch. Robert Vance opines that savaging attacks don't need to be unarmed, as the rules as written dictate, so a Mantis grappler can clash pairs of her Style's weapons against the razor claws of a Tiger grappler.<br /> <br /> Crushing Claw Technique is a nice aid for winning a Clash (for which Tiger Style has no answer), but not with a withering attack. That\u2019s fine, since Mantis doesn\u2019t have a trick that depends on denying the opponent a chance to act between attacks.<br /> <br /> If your opponent is intimidated by your delay and successfully disengages rather than attack you, use Leaping Mantis Technique to chase them down. I don\u2019t think you can delay the reflexive attack, and there\u2019s generally no reason to delay with the alternative, unblockable attack.<br /> <br /> If they instead resort to a Full Defense to deny you a clash, Crushing Claw Technique can help you get around that with a normal attack, as can using a nunchaku or seven-section staff with its Flexible tag. Alternatively, you can use your action to Aim now, for your attack or clash in the next round.<br /> <br /> If your opponent is currently out of reach, there\u2019s no reason to delay using Leaping Mantis Technique.<br /> <br /> Grasping Mantis Defense is great for when <i>you\u2019re</i> the one at the Initiative disadvantage and you can\u2019t trust your Iron Arm Block to protect you. Celestial Exalted who have the Initiative advantage also have the option of making an immediate withering attack to build up more Initiative, and then using GMD to clash when their slower opponent attacks. But that relies on him attacking instead of anything else. Though, again, Mantis Style has options for responding to a Full Defense or Disengage action.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s no reason to delay using Joint-Locking Technique.<br /> <br /> You can Clash with Joint-Breaking Attack, if you really need to neutralize your opponent\u2019s action and are confident you will win. If you\u2019ve already broken one arm of someone who relies on a two-handed weapon, you should be pretty confident about clashing, whether you\u2019re clinching or not.<br /> <br /> <br /> In conclusion, Mantis is much more flexible about parrying or clashing for defense than Tiger Style, having tools for both and leaving you to decide which is best to use at any given moment.<br /> <br /> It should be noted that even if you consistently clash your opponent rather than parrying, Mantis' parrying tricks are still extremely useful for protecting you from a second opponent who is also attacking you, especially while you are clinching the first opponent.<br /> <br /> .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 08-09-2019, 11:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T11:51:20-07:00","id":1244234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1243700-how-often-do-you-delay-your-action-to-attempt-a-clash?p=1244219#post1244219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, as I might make a Snake Stylist in future, and my friend is playing one now.<br /> <br /> I admit, I didn't really think much about clashing with my Tiger Stylist, but you're right, defensively it's not great so clashing really does make sense. Though his initiative isn't that great (Join Battle 6, no excellency). Still, initiative's go up and down through combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m glad this thread helped. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't quite agree that you should always delay and clash though. After all, if you want to make a decisive attack, and they clash you with a light withering attack, they may well have 4 more dice than you. </div> </div> </div>Right, thanks. <br /> <br /> Forgot about decisive attacks lacking accuracy bonuses. But other bonuses such as the Clash bonus of paired and two-handed weapons are still valid.<br /> <br /> Natural weapons don\u2019t get a paired bonus, so a non paired light weapon would only have a 2 dice basic advantage, before other traits.<br /> <br /> A pair of light weapons could have a base advantage of 6 or 7 withering attack dice against a clashing decisive attack which has no bonus. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, of course, in a fight with multiple people, they may attack someone else, at which point you attack them anyway, but wasted 2i. </div> </div> </div>True, but my primary focus is on duels, to keep things simple for comparison.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T12:51:17-07:00","id":1244250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1243700-how-often-do-you-delay-your-action-to-attempt-a-clash?p=1244234#post1244234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True, but my primary focus is on duels, to keep things simple for comparison.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel that this focus unfortunately is systemically flawed, I have very rarely seen in play duels factoring heavily in games either discussed here or in my own experience. This is not to say that there isn\u2019t something valuable being discussed, but proscriptive focuses should account for the majority of actual play experience. Your insights into clashing are absolutely relevant in a one on one context, but the minute multiple combatants enter the picture the arguement breaks down. This is important because I would posit that multiple combat interactions and coordination can render this style of play frustrating or against the player\u2019s expectations.<br /> <br /> Edit: this may have come across as overly harsh, so I do want to thank you for having done this thread it\u2019s been both informative and interesting, i just wish to caution against duel based extrapolations in multiple combatant settings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","user":"Saipjas","date":". 08-09-2018, 03:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T13:38:06-07:00","id":1244260,"title":"","content":"I find duels reasonably common... for Martial Artists. Not so much for Melee or Brawl though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T13:57:17-07:00","id":1244267,"title":"","content":"Well, yeah. That\u2019s definitely one reason why I\u2019m focusing on the basic rules or on Martial Arts Styles, as opposed to Exalted Charmsets.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s easier to envision duels between martial artists, and the closed Charmsets are easier to analyze. It\u2019s a good place to start.<br /> <br /> Plus, I\u2019m trying to develop new Styles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 08-09-2018, 04:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T15:07:51-07:00","id":1244284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1243700-how-often-do-you-delay-your-action-to-attempt-a-clash?p=1244041#post1244041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about when you're delaying to make a smash attack? You're losing a total of 4i.<br /> <br /> It's probably worth every point if it succeeds, but it's still expensive.</div> </div> </div> </div>The character I was using couldn't make those, so not sure. I think you'd tend to about break even on initiative, so maybe still a net plus if you're fighting alongside someone who can take advantage of the brief -2 to their Defense, or can use the environment to make the knockback work for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T15:55:46-07:00","id":1244305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1243700-how-often-do-you-delay-your-action-to-attempt-a-clash?p=1244160#post1244160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't know that it was going under revision, or paid any real attention as to how it compares to the other trees.<br /> <br /> I hope it doesn't get too downgraded, but we'll see!<br /> <br /> Thanks for the info!</div> </div> </div> </div>The core function of the Charm should remain intact. The problem seems to have been how it added (Performance) dice to any movement action on top of that, which placed in competition with both Effortlessly Rising Flame and Threshold Warding Stance, both of which instead add successes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T16:02:48-07:00","id":1244307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1243700-how-often-do-you-delay-your-action-to-attempt-a-clash?p=1244284#post1244284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The character I was using couldn't make those, so not sure. I think you'd tend to about break even on initiative, so maybe still a net plus if you're fighting alongside someone who can take advantage of the brief -2 to their Defense, or can use the environment to make the knockback work for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you attack first with a hammer in a clashing smash attack, succeed, and choose to knockdown instead of knockback, then your ally can enjoy a total of -4 parry or -5 evasion penalty. <br /> <br /> The clash penalty, prone penalty, and onslaught penalty. Not counting any wound penalties if the smash was decisive.<br /> <br /> If the attack was withering, and you steal at least three Initiative points, you can act before your target in the next round and exploit that vulnerability yourself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 08-09-2018, 07:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T06:19:11-07:00","id":1244466,"title":"","content":"Did we ever find out what happens if you clash a multi attack charm? Do you both just clash as many attacks as you have, and then overflow the rest as normal attacks? If that\u2019s the case the fire sig in melee could be used to great effect by delaying to clash, clashing, winning the clash and stacking an onslaught penalty, giving him a total of -3 and -4 to the Defense of the other 2 attacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T07:35:21-07:00","id":1244486,"title":"","content":"Sounds like that's the best way to do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T07:39:15-07:00","id":1244488,"title":"","content":"My general interpretation is that the winner of [whatever you're doing] determines the effects. <br /> <br /> So if you're receiving a multi-attack and Clash it successfully, you'd have stopped the remainder of the attack by pulling it into your Clash. <br /> <br /> If you Clash and lose, the multi-attack multi's right along, according to the attacker's intent.<br /> <br /> Probably not orthogonal to the details in Core, but that's how I'd reason it in the course of play.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T08:20:55-07:00","id":1244501,"title":"","content":"The serpent who holds herself in readiness to strike one opponent forfeits the benefits of her full evasiveness against the attack of a second opponent. In system terms, delaying your action to clash the slower of two opponents means that you cannot use the full power of Serpentine Evasion against the attack of the faster opponent. The Charm is, of course, completely useless in a clash.<br /> <br /> As long as your Initiative remains higher than your target's despite the cost of delaying, Snake Form will penalize your enemy's clash dice by -3, and Striking Cobra Technique will reward you for succeeding at a clash attack. Striking Cobra Technique is more forgiving in terms of Initiative comparisons when used by Solars, or after any Exalt delivers the Essence Venom Strike (which will also ensure Snake Form inflicts the full penalty).<br /> <br /> Snake seems incapable of grappling.<br /> <br /> Snake's best weapons for clashing are the paired hook swords, which have the disarming tag (and taking away your opponent\u2019s weapon is great for clashing), and also provide the +1 parry bonus of medium-weight weapons. The Style\u2019s other weapon, the seven section staff, is similarly defensive. It also has the flexible tag for striking people who choose to Full Defense instead of clashing you.<br /> <br /> Snake Style allows light armor, and Charms such as Snake Form Essence Fangs and Scales Technique, and Countless Coils Evasion provide further precaution against failing a clash.<br /> <br /> Since Countless Coil Evasion doesn't care which form of defense you used, Snake is extremely flexible in regards to whether you want to dodge, parry, or clash, with improved soak to survive failing at any of them. However, Terrestrials are encouraged to dodge (and dodge successfully) if they want to use Crippling Pressure-Point Strike apart from Snake Strikes The Heel.<br /> <br /> Snake Strikes The Heel allows the martial artist to defensively clash, when she is at the Initiative disadvantage. Snake Form helps with a -1 penalty against the opponent. If the martial artist delivered Essence Venom Strike to the opponent, then Snake Form inflicts the full -3 penalty (plus the -2 penalty from the venom itself), and the martial artist can use Striking Cobra Technique and (if a Solar) the Mastery bonus of Essence Fangs and Scales Technique.<br /> <br /> Celestial Exalted can instead use Snake Strikes the Heel while at higher Initiative, to intercept an attack the opponent makes after their own.<br /> <br /> Because Crippling Pressure-Point Strike is a gambit rather than a withering attack, it doesn't lend itself to the same &quot;two action combo&quot; as something like &quot;Stillness-of-Stone Atemi and Avalanche Method&quot;, and Dragon-Blooded are greatly restricted in when they can even use it and cannot use Withering Paralysis Venom. But Celestial Exalted and Immaculates who deliver the Withering Venom Paralysis don't have to worry about their victims fully rising from prone even if they succeed at the action, so the window of opportunity is large.<br /> <br /> Using Nerve-Deadening Venom Atemi against dual wielders and two-handed weapon users can really help your chances of winning clashes, especially with Snake Form.<br /> <br /> Blinding Fang Strike creates the smallest window of opportunity, and I wouldn't allow its penalties to stack with those of Snake Form, since the opponent cannot be hypnotized by movements they cannot see.<br /> <br /> <br /> Uncoiling Serpent Prana. You can use this to clash projectile attacks out to short range. Medium range, if you're a Celestial Exalt who has Essence Scales and Fangs Technique active.<br /> <br /> Your attack isn't treated like a projectile, so your bare hands and feet still have a close range weapon's accuracy of 4. A short range, Thrown weapons have an accuracy of 3/4. Archery weapons match or exceed your hands at 4/5, but at medium range, your unarmed attack has better accuracy than artifact bows.<br /> <br /> Using paired hook swords is also an option, like always. Artifact hook swords will have better clash attack dice pools than your bare hands, better damage, and potentially Evocations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 08-11-2018, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T09:43:47-07:00","id":1244525,"title":"","content":"Shucks, I forgot that I hadn\u2019t covered clashing with the long range attack Charm.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Fixed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 08-09-2019, 10:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T14:09:32-07:00","id":1244615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>autXautY</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1243700-how-often-do-you-delay-your-action-to-attempt-a-clash?p=1244198#post1244198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not the person this is asking, but my analysis of the corebook sidereal excellency and clashes:<br /> <br /> Sidereal excellency is 1m per die or target number reduction, max of (essence) dice and 3 target number reduction. 2m per static number increase, max (essence).<br /> At &gt;5 die pools, target number reduction is more efficient than dice adding, and for most possible essence/attribute/ability/other sources of dice the cap is higher than solars. (At e3+ the sidereal always has a higher cap for expected successes, at e1 or e2 a near max attribute+ability can beat the sidereal if there aren't many dice from stunt, speciality, accuracy, or similar coming in.)<br /> The static excellency, on the other hand, has the same efficiency as everyone else, and at low essence a pretty poor cap.<br /> <br /> This lets them do much better on rolls than other splats before charms, and often even after charms, especially on things like withering attacks with high-accuracy weapons. Clashes put a lot of focus on winning a single roll, can get a lot of non-charm dice from accuracy and dual wielding, and compensate for the sidereal's poor Defense cap.<br /> An e1, dex 5, ability 5, specialty sidereal dual wielding light artifact weapons in a clash with a 1-point stunt and max excellency averages 16.8 successes. And only spends 4m for this<br /> A solar under the same conditions averages 15, excellent strike brings that up to 16.556, for 10 or 11 motes.<br /> At higher essence this gets even more extreme - e5 gives 20 average successes for 8m.<br /> <br /> Because of this, a clash-specialized sidereal can win lots of clashes, even against other clash-specialized enemies, and won't need to spend as many motes.<br /> <br /> On another note, do people think Snake Form's penalty to attacks applies to clash attacks?</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically this, but with more emphasis on how weak PC level Sidereals are defensively without it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T14:18:26-07:00","id":1244620,"title":"","content":"Their Dodge and Melee trees could have Defense Charms to cover those holes.<br /> <br /> I doubt that Sidereals are going to be heavily encouraged to dual wield or two-hand large weapons.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, I have a newfound respect for how Earth Dragon Style just lets you punch someone to help you actually hit them when you\u2019re alone with no onslaught penalties to exploit for your hammer. <br /> <br /> Force of the Mountain helps make up for the difference in damage, and Stillness of Stone\u2019s mobility penalties can make a dodge-reliant opponent an easier target for that smash attack if you steal enough Initiative to act first next round.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T20:03:37-07:00","id":1244709,"title":"","content":"I've asked Robert these questions, and am awaiting his response:<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>If a player decides to Delay their action, and after paying the Initiative cost still has a higher Initiative than the character she wants to clash, does she get to wait until after her target's player declares his actions before deciding which of her own to take, to reflect/reward her advantage?<br /> <br /> The opposite would be if Delaying her action actually puts her Initiative below his, allowing her to act on the same time, but forcing her to declare her actions first so that he may react to her, instead.<br /> <br /> The medium would be if their Initiative scores end up exactly equal, and the matter of who declares first is decided with a coinflip or dice-roll.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> I didn't ask him about when actions are resolved, though.<br /> <br /> Personally, I feel that Disengage actions should be resolved last, Attacks before Disengages, and everything else before Attacks.<br /> <br /> That is, regardless of who declares their action first, something like a Full Defense goes into effect before an attack roll.<br /> <br /> <br /> Do you feel that Rushes should be resolved before Disengages, or that rolled movement actions in general should be resolved last (with reflexive Move actions happening first, in cases where the characters aren't in the same range band?)... or something else?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-11T04:43:18-07:00","id":1244779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1243700-how-often-do-you-delay-your-action-to-attempt-a-clash?p=1244099#post1244099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are my Clash breakdowns of the Martial Arts Styles helpful or interesting at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't speak for anyone else, but I'm lapping them up. I hadn't really considered this. I'd love to hear your thoughts on Dreaming Pearl Courtesan Style if you have the time &amp; inclination.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24421-katamari_naneke","name":"Katamari_Naneke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-11T06:40:59-07:00","id":1244796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1243700-how-often-do-you-delay-your-action-to-attempt-a-clash?p=1244620#post1244620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their Dodge and Melee trees could have Defense Charms to cover those holes.</div> </div> </div> </div>We'll see. But right now there's been efforts to weaken their TN reduction without going &quot;wait, isn't (essence) a horrible defensive cap unless you're an elder?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-11T06:57:12-07:00","id":1244799,"title":"","content":"Okay. A breakdown of the Dreaming Pearl Courtesan's clash potential:<br /> <br /> Things don't look good at the start. No armor to help you survive failed clashes, and no weapons at all. If I didn't mention it before, Robert clarified that bare hands do <i>not</i> enjoy a clash bonus for being paired. The Style's very first Charms do something to make up for that.<br /> <br /> Pearlescent Filigree Defense is cheap and reflexive, but only makes mundane light armor without the Form, which we'll address later. Just on its own, though, the Charm lets you spend further motes to increase soak against a successful withering attack, and if your clashing opponent used a decisive attack (and it's the first decisive attack that hits you in the fight) you get a great boost to toughness.<br /> <br /> Elegant Weapon Repertoire is a supplemental Charm, but since it supplements a draw weapon action, and everyone is allowed a reflexive draw weapon action at Join Battle unless they were ambushed, I would rule that you could use this Charm then to have a fully-readied weapon before anyone acts. I would also rule that you could ready two objects at once, so long as they are functionally identical enough to operate as a pair and thus enjoy the clash bonus. This lets you enchant BOTH sleeves of your long-sleeved robe, or two fans, or a pair of hair-pin sticks. As paired light-weight weapons, they now offer you the second-best clash potential in the game. The Mastery effect and alternative effect don't help win clashes, but do help take advantage of success.<br /> <br /> Okay, it took two whole Charm purchases/activations, but now the DPC is armed for battle when everyone else around her might have thought her completely unequipped and unready to fight. No one can make that mistake now, since her clothes shine with magic and she's brandishing a pair of broken glass-bottle shivs in a fighting stance.<br /> <br /> If she faces one opponent who beat her Join Battle roll and delays, but she's desperate enough to try clashing him anyway, she's got decent equipment for the attempt.<br /> <br /> If she faces one or many opponents and beats them all on the Join Battle roll, but did not ambush them, she could delay her action and wait for one of them to attack her, so that she could clash them. If none of them attack her, she could use the reprieve to assume the Dreaming Pearl Courtesan Form, or perhaps attempt disengaging, which could put her at a safe distance and also possibly let her assume the form reflexively. Using Demure Carp Feint and Seven Storms Escape Prana helps with the later option, especially if the martial artist invested in the complementary Ability of Dodge, along with any Disengage-assisting native Charms.<br /> <br /> Rather than clashing or delaying at all, she may be best off simply Disengaging at the start, if necessary, or using a Full Defense. It depends on how her attack pool compares to her Defense values, give or take the assistance of Demure Carp Feint. As always, the secondary effect of Demure Carp Feint can help off-set the Initiative cost of a Disengage action to help her avoid losing the Initiative advantage, especially with the Mastery effect.<br /> <br /> None of the weapons she can prepare with Elegant Weapon Repertoire will give her a +1 to Defense, and the Style includes no Charms to assist with parrying. Parrying is only an equal or better option compared to Dodging if you've invested more dots in this Style's fundamental Ability than in the Dodge Ability.<br /> <br /> The Form Charm helps with clashes, as it not only allows you to improve the basic traits of your armor and weapons, it allows you to clash at range. If you maintain your distance and your opponent is left with no better options than clumsily throwing sundry objects at you, if it comes to a clash attack, your dice pool is probably much higher. But if they have no ranged option, then they're not likely to give you an opportunity for clash, preferring to Full Defense or attempt to escape to more favorable ground.<br /> <br /> If, on the other hand, they <i>are</i> equipped for ranged attacks, and you find yourself in a clash, you're much better off than naked, even if you're only wearing a bedsheet and holding two pillows.<br /> <br /> Additionally, your ranged weapon attacks are <i>not</i> treated like Thrown attacks, so your accuracy bonus at short range remains unchanged from 4/5. Meanwhile, anyone forced to use Thrown weapons against you only has an accuracy bonus of 3/4 at short range, and Archery weapons can only match your 4/5. Also, don't forget your +2 clash bonus for dual-wielding pillows. Enjoy.<br /> <br /> Flurry of August Leaves and Vindictive Concubine's Pillow Book can reward you for winning a clash, but won't help you succeed at one. Though, you definitely could set yourself up for a better clash result by using Flurry of August Leaves to help disarm someone before the clash, leaving them without their best attack pool.<br /> <br /> Fragant Petal Fascination Kata's ability to give you a higher Initiative total than any number of your enemies can put you into a position where you can delay to clash, or alternatively protect you from clashes by denying them the choice.<br /> <br /> Seven Storms Escape Prana helps the martial artist avoid clashes where she has the disadvantage, by denying close-range specialists the use of their best weapons and by avoiding grapples which would penalize her attack rolls. The Charm also makes it even easier to reflexively assume the Style's Form Charm, and thus gain the clashing potential of light artifact weapons, and the failure-insurance of light artifact armor, as well as the ability to clash projectile attacks.<br /> <br /> After invoking the chimera's coils...<br /> <br /> You can fucking fly. Maintaining your distance just got a lot easier, which really helps for only needing to clash projectiles if you have enough room to ascend even one range band above the ground.<br /> <br /> Then there's Demure Carp Feint and Seven Storms Escape Prana.<br /> <br /> If you didn't already have a weapon readied with Elegant Weapon Repertoire, you automatically gain a light artifact weapon with any of the four associated tags that you want. So, even if you already have a specifically-tagged weapon readied, you can reflexively ready any permissible weapon you can imagine.<br /> <br /> Any armor you've enchanted or will enchant with Pearlescent Filigree Defense gains the traits of medium artifact armor, with no mobility penalty. Much better for failed clashes, with no downside.<br /> <br /> Capitalizing on a successful clash attack gets better with Flurry of August Leaves and Vindictive Concubine's Pillow Book .<br /> <br /> Fragant Petal Fascination Kata now it works even better at helping you gain the option to delay and clash, but remember that you can't use it if you've already used it once in the fight.<br /> <br /> However, if you activated this Charm because you lost your last -2 health level, now you've got an even higher risk for failing a clash. If your opponent can sufficiently overcome your attack dice and your armor, succeeding with a decisive attack lets him inflict one automatic level of health track damage <i>after</i> damage is rolled. So he can utterly fail his damage roll and you will still automatically die, instantly.<br /> <br /> Thankfully, that clash bonus specifies &quot;rolled&quot;, so if your Hardness is good enough, it's good enough. Also, there's the option of post-roll damage reduction effects, like Snake Style's Countless Coils Evasion, or one of those native Dodge Charms you are encouraged to complete the Style with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 08-14-2018, 09:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-11T07:08:38-07:00","id":1244802,"title":"","content":"I just added two paragraphs in the middle regarding using Defense instead of clashing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-11T07:09:13-07:00","id":1244804,"title":"","content":"You can also Invoke the Chimera's Coils at Initiative 15+, which is the only time you should probably do it if you don't want to lose your character, unless you've got a perfect defense banked somewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-11T07:11:14-07:00","id":1244805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cheshire Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1243700-how-often-do-you-delay-your-action-to-attempt-a-clash?p=1244804#post1244804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can also Invoke the Chimera's Coils at Initiative 15+, which is the only time you should probably do it if you don't want to lose your character, unless you've got a perfect defense banked somewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I misread that.<br /> <br /> Also, I misread that you need to already be in the Form.<br /> <br /> I'll fix that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-11T07:17:09-07:00","id":1244807,"title":"","content":"No worries, I still greatly appreciate the work you put into these posts. I generally don't over-analyse the crunch aspect of games, but every few sessions at the table, there's that moment where the &quot;gamey&quot; aspect of play also is a lot of fun, and you just kind of want to tactically optimize your approach. So it's really nice for lazy players like me to have someone else put a lot of thought into this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-11T09:01:26-07:00","id":1244829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cheshire Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1243700-how-often-do-you-delay-your-action-to-attempt-a-clash?p=1244807#post1244807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No worries, I still greatly appreciate the work you put into these posts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't understand the &quot;Like&quot; culture on this website.<br /> <br /> A few people have posted that they appreciate my work, but only one of the posts was Liked. You'll notice that earlier, I had to actually ask if anyone cared what I was doing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-11T09:28:07-07:00","id":1244834,"title":"","content":"\u201cThis could actually incentivize the martial artist (when not clinching) to delay until after his opponent acts, without clashing. She lets her opponent\u2019s attack crash against her Iron Arm Block and suffer an onslaught penalty that makes attacking him easier.\u201d<br /> <br /> Why didn\u2019t anyone call me on this brain fart?<br /> <br /> A better idea is the Mantis stylist using a Full Defense to make sure Iron Arm Block works in the first place, and then attacking first in the next round before the attacker\u2019s new onslaught penalty disappears.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s the same gamble, but less risky and less expensive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 08-11-2018, 12:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-11T09:52:51-07:00","id":1244839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1243700-how-often-do-you-delay-your-action-to-attempt-a-clash?p=1244488#post1244488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My general interpretation is that the winner of [whatever you're doing] determines the effects. <br /> <br /> So if you're receiving a multi-attack and Clash it successfully, you'd have stopped the remainder of the attack by pulling it into your Clash. <br /> <br /> If you Clash and lose, the multi-attack multi's right along, according to the attacker's intent.<br /> <br /> Probably not orthogonal to the details in Core, but that's how I'd reason it in the course of play.</div> </div> </div> </div>If someone has paid for a multi-attack and you haven\u2019t, I feel you should only be able to Clash the first attack.<br /> <br /> Some multi-attacks cease after the first miss, so successfully clashing the first would already shut the rest down.<br /> <br /> Killing the multi-attacker after the first damage resolution should generally also stop the rest of the attacks.<br /> <br /> Crashing the multi-attacker could also work, if his attacks are all decisive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-11T09:54:27-07:00","id":1244840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1243700-how-often-do-you-delay-your-action-to-attempt-a-clash?p=1244834#post1244834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why didn\u2019t anyone call me on this brain fart?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe because when someone corrected an error of yours on the first page, you left a message on their profile about how their nitpicking habits would &quot;catch up with&quot; them?<br /> <br /> \u200bJust a guess, mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 08-11-2018, 12:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-11T10:11:19-07:00","id":1244844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1243700-how-often-do-you-delay-your-action-to-attempt-a-clash?p=1244840#post1244840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe because when someone corrected an error of yours on the first page, you left a message on their profile about how their nitpicking habits would &amp;quot;catch up with&amp;quot; them?<br /> <br /> \u200bJust a guess, mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you\u2019re just ignoring the other people who pointed out problems and to whom I immediately admitted fault and made corrections.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-11T10:27:15-07:00","id":1244848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1243700-how-often-do-you-delay-your-action-to-attempt-a-clash?p=1244844#post1244844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you\u2019re just ignoring the other people who pointed out problems and to whom I immediately admitted fault and made corrections.</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<span style=\"color:white\">[/10chars]</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-11T20:49:26-07:00","id":1245047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1243700-how-often-do-you-delay-your-action-to-attempt-a-clash?p=1244848#post1244848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No.<span style=\"color:white\">[/10chars]</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps you should ask yourself why your post merited a unique response compared to that of others.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, I'm re-writing Mantis and planning on taking another look at Earth Dragon Style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T16:43:29-07:00","id":1245229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1243700-how-often-do-you-delay-your-action-to-attempt-a-clash?p=1244709#post1244709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've asked Robert these questions, and am awaiting his response:<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>If a player decides to Delay their action, and after paying the Initiative cost still has a higher Initiative than the character she wants to clash, does she get to wait until after her target's player declares his actions before deciding which of her own to take, to reflect/reward her advantage?<br /> <br /> The opposite would be if Delaying her action actually puts her Initiative below his, allowing her to act on the same time, but forcing her to declare her actions first so that he may react to her, instead.<br /> <br /> The medium would be if their Initiative scores end up exactly equal, and the matter of who declares first is decided with a coinflip or dice-roll.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> I didn't ask him about when actions are resolved, though.<br /> <br /> Personally, I feel that Disengage actions should be resolved last, Attacks before Disengages, and everything else before Attacks.<br /> <br /> That is, regardless of who declares their action first, something like a Full Defense goes into effect before an attack roll.<br /> <br /> <br /> Do you feel that Rushes should be resolved before Disengages, or that rolled movement actions in general should be resolved last (with reflexive Move actions happening first, in cases where the characters aren't in the same range band?)... or something else?</div> </div> </div> </div>Did anyone have any thoughts on this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T19:28:42-07:00","id":1245288,"title":"","content":"Rush vs. Disengage is a pretty niche case. The timing of their resolution only matters if both parties are acting on the same tick (which I do realize is the theme of this whole thread), and even then it only matters in a few very specific scenarios:<br /> <br /> 1.) Without Charms, Rush vs. Disengage only happens if Character A and Character B are in Close Range of each other (or A moves into Close Range with her Reflexive Move before B declares his actions), and then one of the following cases occurs: a.) A declares actions first, <i>guesses</i> that B is going to try to Disengage, declares a Rush, and then B actually does declare a Disengage, b.) B declares actions first, declares a Disengage, and then A declares a Rush to try to counter it, or c.) if actions are declared simultaneously, A guesses that B is going to Disengage and declares a Rush to try to counter it, and is proven correct.<br /> <br /> In scenarios 1a. and 1c. I would have no qualms with rolling the Rush first. If either action fails, the resolution is obvious. If both the Rush (rolled first) and the Disengage (rolled second) succeed, my interpretation is that the Disengager would move out to Short Range, then the Rush's reflexive movement would trigger and move the Rusher back into Close Range, and then... the phrasing is trickier, but I think a common-sense interpretation would allow the Disengage's reflexive movement to trigger, allowing the Disengager to move back to Short Range<i>. </i><i>Ultimately</i>, however, unless a third party intervenes, the Rusher wins that exchange, since the Disengager had to spend Initiative to get away from her, meaning the Rusher's turn will come up next, and the Disengager's reflexive moment from winning a Disengage is already spent.<br /> <br /> Scenario 1b. is slightly trickier, but only slightly. If B declared his Disengage first, I might be inclined to roll it first. In that case, if B wins, he moves to Short Range before A's Rush is rolled. A can still Rush from Short Range, but since B's movement occurred before the Rush was rolled, no further movement would happen on this round even if the Rush succeeds. If the Rush failed, the resolution would be obvious, but if the Rush succeeded, and there was no outside interference with Initiative, A's turn would come up first on the next round. If A then moved from Short into Close Range with her Reflexive move, B's Reflexive move from Disengage would trigger, moving him back to Short, then that movement would trigger Rush's Reflexive movement, moving A back into Close. Again, if both the Rusher and Disengager succeed at their rolls on the same tick, and no one else tampers with their Initiative, the Rusher effectively 'wins' the exchange: order of resolution only changes the timing of whether all the movement is concluded on the same round they Rush and Disengage, or if the last of their movement occurs on the next round.<br /> <br /> 2.) I had a bit here talking about edge cases with Charms, but most of them (at least involving Solar Charms) are actually fairly self-evident, with even my slight confusion over Godspeed Steps having been answered in the past by <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1102918#post1102918\">one of your questions to the Ask the Devs thread</a>. My only remaining confusion is Fleet Dreaming Image, and my confusion regarding that Charm is somewhat tangential to the question of this thread, so I think I'm going to ask Ask the Devs instead of expounding on it here.<br /> <br /> The only specific note I'll make is that Sunlight Bleeding Away is a way of answering the &quot;Rusher effectively always wins if both Rusher and Disengager succeed at their actions&quot; issue I noted in part 1, since it would allow the Disengager to win instead in that scenario.<br /> <br /> <u>Alternative</u><u>:</u> This would most certainly be a houserule, but if you wanted quicker resolution and a more definitive result, a Storyteller <i>could</i> choose to resolve an opposed Rush and Disengage on the same tick as a single opposed roll of Dex + Athletics vs. Dex + Dodge instead of two opposed rolls, one of Dex + Athletics vs. Dex + Athletics and one of Dex + Dodge vs. Dex + Athletics. You could then allow <i>only</i> the winner of the contested roll's action to succeed, removing the possibilities of mutual successes or mutual failures. (Incidentally, I will note that a mutual failure would also effectively favor the Rusher, just like a mutual success does, since the Disengager would still end up at Close Range with lower Initiative than the Rusher.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21733-ascension","name":"Ascension","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21733_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-12T21:43:49-07:00","id":1245326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ascension</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1243700-how-often-do-you-delay-your-action-to-attempt-a-clash?p=1245288#post1245288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rush vs. Disengage is a pretty niche case. The timing of their resolution only matters if both parties are acting on the same tick (which I do realize is the theme of this whole thread), and even then it only matters in a few very specific scenarios</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, yes. I see I got myself confused about the <i>resolution </i>of these two actions versus the <i>declaration</i> of those two actions.<br /> <br /> Since both characters are acting on the same tick, neither one should have the ability to declare and resolve an action before the other. If the delaying character wanted to act first, there was no point in delaying. If the delaying character wanted to let the slower character declare and resolve without interruption, she would delay until the tick after the slower character takes her turn.<br /> <br /> As you say, resolution order doesn't matter after both players declare these actions before resolving anything. Only the <i>declaration</i> order is important, because there's no point in trying to rush someone who doesn't try to disengage.<br /> <br /> <br /> Unless... would it be possible to Rush someone in one round, then Smash them into a different range band in the next turn, triggering your own reflexive movement from the Rush to follow them into that range band?<br /> <br /> Looking at the rules as written, there's no time-limit given for a successful Rush. You opponent could wait three rounds to try disengaging, and by the RAW, you'd still reflexively move after them. Only Disengage gives a time-limit of &quot;her next turn&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If both the Rush (rolled first) and the Disengage (rolled second) succeed, my interpretation is that the Disengager would move out to Short Range, then the Rush's reflexive movement would trigger and move the Rusher back into Close Range, and then... the phrasing is trickier, but I think a common-sense interpretation would allow the Disengage's reflexive movement to trigger, allowing the Disengager to move back to Short Range<i>. </i><i>Ultimately</i>, however, unless a third party intervenes, the Rusher wins that exchange, since the Disengager had to spend Initiative to get away from her, meaning the Rusher's turn will come up next, and the Disengager's reflexive moment from winning a Disengage is already spent. </div> </div> </div>And the Rusher will surely start her turn by using her reflexive Movement action to enter close range, which denies the Disengager from using his reflexive Movement on his following turn. And as you say, the Disengager lost Initiative from the exchange equal to the amount the Rusher spent to delay, so they should still be more or less at the same level of advantage. Unless the Disengager crashed himself, and thus gave the Rusher an Initiative Break bonus.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2.) I had a bit here talking about edge cases with Charms, but most of them (at least involving Solar Charms) are actually fairly self-evident, with even my slight confusion over Godspeed Steps having been answered in the past by <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1102918#post1102918\">one of your questions to the Ask the Devs thread</a>. My only remaining confusion is Fleet Dreaming Image, and my confusion regarding that Charm is somewhat tangential to the question of this thread, so I think I'm going to ask Ask the Devs instead of expounding on it here. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Holden and whoever else might have been writing Charms seemed to struggle mightily with the corebook, and various Charms look like they should have gotten another evaluation.<br /> <br /> But ultimately, they did a great job, and any errata would be much less thorough and onerous compared to the previous editions. No need for First Editions &quot;power combat&quot;, or Second Edition's &quot;Dawn Solution&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> But setting that aside, what about my other questions?<br /> <br /> Robert thought it should all come down to a coinflip, but I really do prefer that when a character delays to act in another character's tick, she gets to declare last if her Initiative is still higher after paying the cost, and is forced to declare last if her Initiative fell lower after paying the cost, with a coinflip saved for when both Initiative tracks are equal.<br /> <br /> But I totally understand if that's not a complication anyone else wants to remember.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T23:17:31-07:00","id":1245780,"title":"","content":"Thanks for doing DPC, and for being so thorough with it! I hadn't really thought about all the implications of holding people at short range. It seems a shame to lose the power of contesting disengages if you're winning, but I guess (absent charms) you could always just give chase with regular move actions.<br /> <br /> I can't speak for anyone else on the likes, but I have privacy settings on my browser that keep logging me out. I normally only log in if I want to make a comment.<br /> <br /> I think the lower initiative declaring their action first is the most intuitive solution. Same with going Rush -&gt; Attack -&gt; Disengage, although I haven't really thought much about other combat actions in that mix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24421-katamari_naneke","name":"Katamari_Naneke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T05:22:26-07:00","id":1245832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katamari_Naneke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1243700-how-often-do-you-delay-your-action-to-attempt-a-clash?p=1245780#post1245780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the lower initiative declaring their action first is the most intuitive solution. Same with going Rush -&gt; Attack -&gt; Disengage, although I haven't really thought much about other combat actions in that mix.</div> </div> </div> </div>The most intuitive solution is writing proper rules <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?769698-Exalted-3E-Simple-Questions&amp;p=19556200#post19556200\" target=\"_blank\">https://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php...0#post19556200</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1628-emeraldstreak","name":"emeraldstreak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1628_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T13:47:05-07:00","id":1246042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1243700-how-often-do-you-delay-your-action-to-attempt-a-clash?p=1244848#post1244848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No.<span style=\"color:white\">[/10chars]</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Come on, this is threadcrapping and you know better Alucard. Please don't do this again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T13:57:46-07:00","id":1246425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1243700-how-often-do-you-delay-your-action-to-attempt-a-clash?p=1244799#post1244799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elegant Weapon Repertoire is a supplemental Charm, but since it supplements a draw weapon action, and everyone is allowed a reflexive draw weapon action at Join Battle unless they were ambushed, I would rule that you could use this Charm then to have a fully-readied weapon before anyone acts. I would also rule that you could ready two objects at once, so long as they are functionally identical enough to operate as a pair and thus enjoy the clash bonus. This lets you enchant BOTH sleeves of your long-sleeved robe, or two fans, or a pair of hair-pin sticks. As paired light-weight weapons, they now offer you the second-best clash potential in the game. The Mastery effect and alternative effect don't help win clashes, but do help take advantage of success.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just noticed this paragraph. While I think your rulings would be much more manageable for a DPC stylist, both aesthetically and mechanically, and are probably how the style <i>should</i> be played, the question of whether you could use Elegant Weapon Repertoire at the start of combat came up in my game, I asked Ask The Devs, and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1170783#post1170783\">Vance said no, it strictly requires a Ready Weapon action</a>.<br /> <br /> You can still flurry Ready Weapon, of course, so it's not as limiting as a Simple Charm, but it's disappointing that DPC takes that kind of prep work just to be armed, especially since the style doesn't <i>really</i> come into its own until the Form is up. I definitely think this is one where Orichalcum Rule should take precedence and you should go for what makes the game fun for your player if you have a DPC stylist in your party.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21733-ascension","name":"Ascension","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21733_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T14:15:53-07:00","id":1246429,"title":"","content":"The action can\u2019t be flurried if you wanted your first action to be assuming the Form Charm.<br /> <br /> Flurrying a ready weapon action with a Disengage makes it possible but hard to do both in the same turn.<br /> <br /> <br /> Oh, and I\u2019m getting close to done with the new breakdown of Earth Dragon Style. It\u2019s a beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T20:18:08-07:00","id":1246525,"title":"","content":"<b>Immaculate Earth Dragon Style's clash potential and general tactics Breakdown!</b><br /> <br /> Earth Dragon Style allows the heaviest of armor and provides plenty of toughness in its Charms, so it is well-disposed to survive a clash gone bad. The armor's mobility penalty makes it harder on you if your opponent responds to a delay with a disengage action, and especially if they succeed and you need to rush, so hopefully you can declare a smash attack after they declare disengage, and resolve your smash attack before their disengage is rolled.<br /> <br /> Earth Dragon's tetsubo is a horrible defensive weapon, as it actually penalizes Parry by 1. Artifact equivalents offer a neutral +0, equal to the bare-handed Parries also allowed by the Style. The Style by itself offers no way to parry lethal weapons or projectiles with your bare hands, forcing you to eat a tetsubo's penalty if you don't have an artifact hammer or a Charm like Become the Hammer or Fists of Iron Technique.<br /> <br /> Basically, an Earth Dragon stylist seldom relies on her Defense to avoid getting hit, but just to mitigate the damage of withering attacks before applying her prodigious soak. This is why Stone Dragon's Skin does not bother trying to improve her poor Parry Defense, but merely to keep as much of it as possible, even after previous blows have successfully injured her.<br /> <br /> Clashing is a better defense for the Earth Dragon, when she can manage it. Weapon-Breaking Defense Technique is a rare Charm that allows a Dragon-Blood to make a reflexive clash attack that doesn't count against her action that round or the next, even if any Exalt needs to meet a reset condition to use it more than once in a fight. Weapon-Breaking Defense Technique can't hurt the Earth Dragon's opponent, but it can make following defenses, attacks, and clashes easier since the enemy is deprived of their preferred form of attack and defense.<br /> <br /> Should the Earth Dragon choose to clash with her hands or with her hammer? Her hammer enjoys the +2 clash bonus that gives it just two less dice of basic accuracy than her bare hands (one die less, as an artifact), making it a fair answer to a mundane medium weapon or any sort of heavy weapon. If your opponent would rather Full Defense than clash you, you're better off chancing an unarmed attack. But sometimes, you just really need your clash to be a smashing attack, and Earth Dragon Style isn't compatible with fist weapons.<br /> <br /> Force of the Mountain doesn't directly help win a clash, but helps you capitalize on a win, especially with a successful clash's damage bonus, and if you used the hammer instead of your fist.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clashing and Smashing</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Before we talk about the rest of Earth Dragon's Charms, we need to talk more about how important it is for you, when fighting alone with this Style, to use a clashing withering attack (the &quot;setup&quot; attack) to secure a &quot;followup&quot; attack against a target before they have a chance to act. Two of the Style's Charms absolutely depend on this tactic, if you are forced to fight alone, but each of them merely expand upon the inherent advantages of this tactic.<br /> <br /> Smart opponents will go after your weak Defense rather than challenging you to a clash, which could lead to this strategy only becoming available when you hold the Initiative advantage. Even then, it requires your opponent to dare meeting your attack with an attack instead of attempting a Full Defense or Disengage action.<br /> <br /> Even assuming that they take the dare, they could win; on top of the Initiative you lose or the injuries you take, failing the clash means suffering a total Defense penalty of -3 to both Parry and Evasion from onslaught and clash failure, not counting the Parry penalty from using a mundane tetsubo against a lethal or ranged attack that you can't parry bare-handed (at least without Become the Hammer or Fist of Iron Technique), or counting the Evasion penalty from any armor you're wearing.<br /> <br /> If your enemy has the Initiative advantage after that exchange, they can act first in the next round and exploit all of those penalties on you without needing an ally to do it for them. Without your Defense to mitigate damage, you'll have to rely entirely on the considerable toughness that Earth Dragon Style can provide.<br /> <br /> But if you succeed at the clash, the considerable damage that Earth Dragon can inflict really shines. Plus, it is now your opponent's Defense that will suffer a total -3 Defense penalty. You won't need a second clash attack to improve your chances of landing a hammer blow while they're in that condition, though since you're acting first, you certainly can delay to take the risk. This is an excellent time to make your follow-up attack decisive, but we'll talk more about that later.<br /> <br /> Now we want to factor in smashing attacks, which make this tactic even more risky and somewhat more expensive, but far more powerful. Mote-wise, this advance tactic is actually cheaper if you are using Earth Dragon Form, which adds dice to smashing attacks. The risk comes from the costs of attempting a smash attack, which penalizes your Defense by 1; that brings your Defense penalties for failure up to -4. Further, beware of the fact that delaying to clash and then attempting a smash attack means spending a total of 4i, which punishes you that much more if you lose and makes it that much harder to act first in the next round even if you succeed.<br /> <br /> Not that you need to do better than basic success if knocking your target away sends them over a cliff. That can end the fight right there, without any Charms or follow-up attacks. But absent that or any kind of obstruction (like an ally to keep them embattled in their new range band), merely knocking someone away is worthless. Since they aren't also knocked prone without magic, they can simply take a reflexive Move action to close the distance and attack you without penalty, while your own Defense is penalized by -2 from the onslaught of the clash and the cost of the smash attack.<br /> <br /> In a less tactically interesting environment, it's better to knock your opponent prone. Even if you fail to act first in the next round, your opponent will suffer a -3 attack penalty (one point greater than your Defense penalty) from being prone or from flurrying a rise-from-prone action with an attack. If they fail to rise-from-prone (the difficulty is only 2, but the action suffers a -3 penalty on top of any armor they're wearing) their attack will instead suffer a -6 penalty. A flurry would also penalize their Defense by 1. Also, they can't take a movement action to disengage that turn, one way or another. If they're still prone by the time you attack them, their Parry is reduced by 1 and their Evasion by 2, before adding any penalty for a flurry or for wearing armor.<br /> <br /> But if you succeed well enough to act first in the next round after knocking them down, your opponent's Parry will be penalized by -4, and their Evasion will suffer a -5 penalty even before including any mobility penalties from their armor. Plus, being prone means that any Earth Dragon attack made against them, smashing or otherwise, gets bonus dice. Again: You won't need a second clash attack to improve your chances of landing a hammer blow while they're in that condition, though since you're acting first, you certainly can delay to take the risk. This is an excellent time to make your follow-up attack decisive.<br /> <br /> If you want to make the followup attack a smashing one, now is a better time to consider knocking them away, since they'll still be prone when they land, and thus will be incapable of simply moving back into close range with you on their next turn. That could buy you time to activate a Simple-type power-up Charm, or start running away without needing to disengage. Beware that a decisive smashing attack still costs 2i, so you're effectively reducing your decisive damage pool to buy that time. So without particular Charms, there's no reason to make the follow-up attack a knockdown smash, and if you don't need to buy time, you might as well just make a normal decisive attack.<br /> <br /> Unless, of course, you chose to make a non-smashing attack with the setup withering attack. In which case, they're not already flat on their back, and you're currently in the best position to put them there before you reset yourself to base Initiative, to afford yourself protection from their best efforts to hurt you.<br /> <br /> Perfection of Earth Body makes it easier to shrug off failed clashes and capitalize on successful ones, and further encourages you to smash your target on either the setup attack or followup attack, if not both. However, using the Charm costs you Initiative, and therefore makes it harder to gain enough advantage to delay and clash.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Impudent, Impatient Dragons</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Avalanche Method has an Essence Minimum of 4. If you want solid, Earth-aspected followup attacks to finish an opponent off, there are easier alternatives outside of the Style.<br /> <br /> Rolling Boulder Blow (Brawl 3, Essence 2) is like Avalanche Method Lite, but has the bonus of adding threshold successes on your attack roll (of which you'll have plenty with the above tactics) to your decisive damage pool. Earth Dragon Form cannot assist Brawl attacks, but I dare say that you won't need the discount to Become the Hammer. Also, knocking them out of your range band and prone means that they can't attack you immediately after you reset to base Initiative; they would need to use their movement action to rise from prone, so they can't close the distance with you immediately.<br /> <br /> Firmament-Shattering Impact (Brawl 5, Essence 3) is also cheaper than Avalanche Method, and has similar knockback range/damage potential. It should even be able to work with Hungry Earth Strike like Avalanche Method does.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, now we're ready to talk about Stillness-of-Stone Atemi. This Charm is most powerful and useful in team fights, when you're fighting with an ally against an enemy who relies on Evasion and movement actions. But getting any use out of this Charm when you're alone demands that you understand the advanced tactics described above.<br /> <br /> As a Withering-only Charm, Stillness-of-Stone Atemi is a natural partner to the setup withering attack. It can supplement a bare-handed attack, a hammer attack, or a smashing hammer attack.<br /> <br /> Beware that delaying to use this Charm in a clash costs you 2i, which leaves you with less Initiative to spend on Stillness-of-Stone and still have the Initiative advantage on your opponent. Delaying to use this charm on a smash attack in a clash costs you 4i, which makes it worse. Having that Initiative advantage is important, because unless you crash your target, the mobility penalty will wear off at the beginning of his turn... and also, you'll have failed to take advantage of all the other penalties that you inflicted, which would really suck. It sucks beyond measure if you were trying to setup for Avalanche Method.<br /> <br /> Anyway, if you do succeed in crashing your opponent, you're not only assured to act first in the next round, but you'll also enjoy an Initiative Break bonus that will help a followup decisive attack. Plus, the mobility penalty from Stillness-of-Stone will last until your target recovers from crash, which makes it harder for your target to rise-from-prone, if you knocked them prone with the setup attack or will knock them prone with the followup. It could buy you more time to escape or power-up if you use the followup attack to smash them away after knocking them prone with the setup. Alternatively, it will make it harder for them to disengage from you even as it extends your window of opportunity to destroy them with Avalanche method. And they're just plain screwed if they rely on Evasion for Defense.<br /> <br /> If the target you crashed was a spirit, you can also reflexively slap them with Ghost-Grounding Blow. Beware the Initiative price that could cost you a followup attack.<br /> <br /> A normal clash can be an opportunity to use Shattering Fist Strike instead of Weapon-Breaking Defense Technique, saving you seven motes and the use of the reflexive clash for later in the battle. SFS is a gambit, and can be used as a followup attack if you need your opponent's weapon gone more badly than you need the opportunity to kill them.<br /> <br /> I already talked about WBDT.<br /> <br /> There is no point to delaying Earthshaker Attack, which is unblockable and undodgeable and can\u2019t be clashed. This Charm is one reason why an Earth Dragon Stylist might find herself needing to duel and clash an enemy even when she has allies in the fight, since her friends want to avoid EA's radius. Since EA can knock opponents prone, it's an opportunity to enjoy the benefits of using Earth Dragon Form with a hammer blow against a prone opponent for your setup attack, making it easier to achieve a followup attack.<br /> <br /> Hungry Earth Strike is a powerful setup attack Charm, but the 6i cost strains combination potential. If your target isn't already prone, you need to smash him down, which means using a hammer blow, which means you want to use a clash attack for maximum accuracy (but your target might refuse to clash and force you to roll against their Defense), and that means the total Initiative cost raises to 10i before you start spending any Initiative on Stillness-of-Stone Atemi. At least you don't need to pay the Initiative cost of Ghost-Grounding Blow. Unless you are absolutely sure that you can crash the target with this setup attack, &quot;Delayed Clashing Smash + Stillness-of-Stone Atemi + Hungry Earth Strike&quot; is probably not worth it, especially if the target isn't being smashed into an earthern surface.<br /> <br /> If your target is already prone (perhaps from Earthshaker Attack), you could just make a normal unarmed attack without delay and enjoy the Earth Dragon Form's dice bonus to prone targets, counting on the Overwhelming bonus of Stillness-of-Stone Atemi, the 8-doubling of Hungry Earth Strike, and the raw damage boost of Force of the Mountain (and possibly also Perfection of Earth Body) to make up for the damage potential lost by not using the hammer.<br /> <br /> Stillness-of-Stone Atemi + Hungry Earth Strike could also be used to supplement a withering followup attack, after a relatively cheap setup attack has left the target extremely vulnerable and potentially given you plenty of Initiative to spend. Since Hungry Earth Strike requires crashing the target to achieve its full effect, the mobility penalty of Stillness-of-Stone Atemi would also be extended, which extends your window for using Avalanche Technique so that it doesn't need to be the followup attack.<br /> <br /> Ideally, you use Avalanche Method to murder someone wearing full-plate armor after your buddies wore down his Defense with onslaught. Without any of that, this thing is a headache to access. As a reminder, Hungry Earth Strike does not inflict mobility penalties; nothing in Earth Dragon Style does except for Stillness-of-Stone Atemi.<br /> <br /> If they're not wearing armor, you need a setup attack with Stillness-of-Stone Atemi so that you can use Avalanche Method as the followup attack, or you need to crash them with Stillness-of-Stone, ideally on a followup attack with Hungry Earth Strike.<br /> <br /> If Avalanche Method is used as a direct followup attack for a non-smashing SoSA setup made against a target that wasn't already prone, the target is suffering from a starting Defense penalty of -3. If the target was already prone or the setup made them prone, then the target is suffering from a starting Parry penalty of -4 and Evasion penalty of -5 (plus mobility penalties), and Earth Dragon Form gives you bonus attack dice even if none of your attacks with Avalanche Method are smashing.<br /> <br /> Why would you not want to use smashing attacks with Avalanche Method, especially if you have the target trapped with Hungry Earth Strike? Because smashing attacks still cost Initiative, so each one you use lowers your decisive damage pool. However, the damage pool of each attack can't fall below her base Initiative, so after certain a point, there's nothing more to lose.<br /> <br /> If you wanted to start with a smashing attack, would you need to pay the Initiative before or after activating the Charm? I don't know. If so, you'd need 14+ Initiative.<br /> <br /> You certainly would need 14+ Initiative to delay to attempt clashing with Avalanche Method without starting with a smashing attack. But would you want to delay and clash?<br /> <br /> If you don't have a hammer, then there's no point to delaying; just use your fists or stomp them with your feet. But without the hammer, you can't smash. If you want to smash, you might want the +2 clash bonus, especially if the target is only suffering a -3 Defense penalty at the start. But if they're suffering a -4/-5 penalty... And each attack should inflict another onslaught penalty, which means you could start with a non-clashing punch or two before switching to smashing hammer blows.<br /> <br /> Though the number of attacks you can make is limited by their total mobility penalty. How well did you do with SoSA, and how many penalty points did you dare pay for?<br /> <br /> Do you take the risk that you might miss with any Avalanche attack and lose the rest, or are you currently in Earth Aura and don't need to sweat that?<br /> <br /> Are they even trapped with Hungry Earth Strike? Or is there a fatal fall off a cliff at long range?<br /> <br /> For all that this Charm can be inflexible to access, it can be astoundingly flexible in execution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 08-09-2019, 11:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-15T20:54:02-07:00","id":1246528,"title":"","content":"I'll be sad but understanding if no one wants to read that... thing.<br /> <br /> I did not expect it to get so huge.<br /> <br /> If you want to read it, but find that it looks unreadable, please suggest formatting changes that would make it easier for you to read.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-16T10:10:09-07:00","id":1246681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1243700-how-often-do-you-delay-your-action-to-attempt-a-clash?p=1246528#post1246528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll be sad but understanding if no one wants to read that... thing.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#EE82EE\">I did not expect it to get so huge.</span><br /> <br /> If you want to read it, but find that it looks unreadable, please suggest formatting changes that would make it easier for you to read.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#EE82EE\">*giggle*</span><br /> <br /> I read it and also saved it in my notes. Thank you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-16T10:23:51-07:00","id":1246690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1243700-how-often-do-you-delay-your-action-to-attempt-a-clash?p=1246681#post1246681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#EE82EE\">*giggle*</span><br /> <br /> I read it and also saved it in my notes. Thank you!</div> </div> </div> </div>I just had to go back and correct the bit questioning whether to use your unarmed attack or hammer to clash. The difference is two dice rather than one, if you use a mundane weapon.<br /> <br /> But I\u2019m happy that this monstrosity seems to be helpful, or at least interesting!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-16T10:33:02-07:00","id":1246696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1243700-how-often-do-you-delay-your-action-to-attempt-a-clash?p=1246690#post1246690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But I\u2019m happy that this monstrosity seems to be helpful, or at least interesting!</div> </div> </div> </div>My play group is still finishing up our sci-fi epic... which incidentally has had some Exalted bleed-over. Our ship has sprouted a halo that's not unlike a caste mark, and has an instinctive level AI built in and slowly awakening, which acts in a very aggressive-for-good manner when it has a say in things. And it is, as it turns out, built with ancient technology from moon gods. hmmmmm.....<br /> <br /> Anyway!<br /> <br /> I'm hoping we can have Ex3 as our next big epic Chronicle, and I'd like to include some good DBs as part of that. I have some skeptical players with bad memories of Ex2 DBs, so I definitely want to present them as being competent and fun, even if they wind up in the orbit of the Celestials. <br /> <br /> Since I lack a lot of playtest time at the moment, collecting guides and tips like this is very valuable. Between this and DrLoveMonkey's postings I've opened up a new branch of notes to chew through. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-16T14:36:04-07:00","id":1246751,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m trying to write a two-handed hammer Style that is distinguished from Earth Dragon in relying on mobility and agility rather than toughness, and prefers to play ball with the opponent rather than bury him alive.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s really tricky, especially when my main inspirations currently don\u2019t show us enough of how such a martial artist defends herself against an opponent who acts first.<br /> <br /> Nora (RWBY) and Meru (Legend of Dragoon) are either swinging or being struck, with very little in between.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 08-16-2018, 05:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-19T06:24:15-07:00","id":1247678,"title":"","content":"I confess, I didn't quite make it all the way through that second Earth Dragon Style write-up. I'll have another crack later, it's getting late here.<br /> <br /> I loved Legend of the Dragoon, so I'll go and take a proper look at that martial art later too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24421-katamari_naneke","name":"Katamari_Naneke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-19T08:21:09-07:00","id":1247704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katamari_Naneke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1243700-how-often-do-you-delay-your-action-to-attempt-a-clash?p=1247678#post1247678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I confess, I didn't quite make it all the way through that second Earth Dragon Style write-up. I'll have another crack later, it's getting late here.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a fucking monster. I'm happy that anyone made the attempt, let alone wants to try finishing it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I loved Legend of the Dragoon, so I'll go and take a proper look at that martial art later too. </div> </div> </div>The thread about making <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229666-a-complement-to-earth-dragon-style\">an agile complement to Earth Dragon Style </a>starts with an aborted design.<br /> <br /> If by &quot;martial art&quot; you mean you wanted to watch Meru's &quot;additions&quot;, here's a youtube video of her spinning hammer dance: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=C0NpaGi6xi4\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=C0NpaGi6xi4</a><br /> <br /> The thread with the aborted design contains other video links, such as for Nora (<i>RWBY</i>) and also two different two-handed hammer styles featured in <i>Warfame</i>.<br /> <br /> There's also Wise Old Guru's new attempt at the concept: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1247566-peach-dancing-tsunami-style-or-you-want-a-spinny-flippy-hammer-style-here\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...mer-style-here</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 08-19-2018, 11:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T07:15:01-07:00","id":1249123,"title":"","content":"It is interesting to consider clashes, setup attacks, and followup attacks with heavy weapons that lack the smashing tag. Great swords and axes aren\u2019t any more accurate than mauls, and their greater potential for damage doesn\u2019t matter if they can\u2019t hit their targets. It\u2019s easier to hit a target you managed to knock prone, so the hammer effectively becomes more accurate after succeeding once.<br /> <br /> I think a Martial Art using great swords and axes might need to answer this puzzle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T07:19:07-07:00","id":1249128,"title":"","content":"Just a quick question. You can clash a decisive with a withering right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T07:30:19-07:00","id":1249130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1243700-how-often-do-you-delay-your-action-to-attempt-a-clash?p=1249128#post1249128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a quick question. You can clash a decisive with a withering right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. It seems most reflexive Clash Charms are Decisive-only to force you to question whether you want to blow your Initiative to defend instead of Defend, but the keyword doesn\u2019t mean that you can only use such Charms against decisive attacks.<br /> <br /> A reflexive Clash Charm that let you use a withering atttack would be much less risky, especially since you could use your Accuracy bonus in the attack pool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T08:10:40-07:00","id":1249139,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the lack of any kind of restriction on Thousand Strikes Dance and the ability to use it vs. multiple opponents is why Ahlat is the Pattycake Champion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a hre